.TH garuda-toolbox-bootrepair-regenerate 1  "garuda-toolbox 6.3.0" 
.SH NAME
garuda\-toolbox\-bootrepair\-regenerate \- Build the boot files of an installed system again: GRUB\*(Aqs menu, or systemd\-boot\*(Aqs kernel images
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgaruda\-toolbox bootrepair regenerate\fR [\fB\-\-passphrase\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-\-boot\-repair\fR] [\fB\-\-trust\-disk\fR] [\fB\-\-layout\fR \fILAYOUT\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISYSTEM\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Build the boot files of an installed system again: GRUB\*(Aqs menu, or systemd\-boot\*(Aqs kernel images
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-passphrase\-stdin\fR
A locked system\*(Aqs passphrase is asked on the terminal without echo, or read from the first line of standard input with this
.TP
\fB\-\-boot\-repair\fR
Run on an installed system too, for testing. The helper still refuses a disk the running system uses
.TP
\fB\-\-trust\-disk\fR
Outside the live ISO, run the chosen system\*(Aqs own grub\-install, mkinitcpio and bootctl as root. Anyone who could write to that disk could put code there
.TP
\fB\-\-layout\fR \fI<LAYOUT>\fR
Where the system lies on a btrfs or encrypted partition: `plain` at its top, or `subvolume` in Garuda\*(Aqs `@`. Without it `@`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
plain
.IP \(bu 2
subvolume
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the programs\*(Aq own words under an error
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Do not ask, carry the change out. Needed without a terminal
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the plan and stop, without asking and without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print long text directly instead of through `$PAGER`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Colour the output: auto, always or never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON Lines instead of text, for scripts. Needs `\-\-yes` or `\-\-dry\-run`
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<COLUMNS>\fR
Cut long cells to this many columns
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Leave out the spinner and the hints
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISYSTEM\fR>
The installed system\*(Aqs device, as `bootrepair show` prints it
.SH EXTRA
Example:
  garuda\-toolbox bootrepair regenerate /dev/nvme0n1p2
.SH "SEE ALSO"
garuda\-toolbox\-bootrepair(1), garuda\-toolbox(1)
